  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through Tuesday) \nIssued at 1250 AM CDT Wed Sep 30 2026\n\nAfter an active period of weather on Wednesday and Thursday, we will \nsee the strong low pressure systems exit our area by Friday. \nHowever, we will still be under a weak trough through the weekend. \nThis will allow the heavier rain to subside and alleviate flood \nconcerns quite a bit but not completely. A Marginal Risk (5 to 15% \nchance) for seeing excessive rainfall leading to flash flooding is \nstill in place for Friday. Medium chances (40-60%) for rain will \nremain in the forecast, especially across areas east of a Abilene to \nSonora line. Additional rainfall amounts of around a half an inch \n(0.50\") are possible through Sunday. Then, long range models \nredevelop a high pressure system across the southwestern U.S. for \nearly next week, which will leave us under its influence. Drier \nconditions will result and highs are forecast to be in the upper 70s \nto lower 80s.",
